[Unit]
Description=MIA Homestead emergency auto-rollback (crash-loop trigger)
# This is the layer core/deploy_manager.py's app-level watch (started via
# core/deploy_cli.py --start-watch after a deploy) cannot cover on its
# own: if the process won't even start, there's no live Python watching
# alerts to make that judgment -- systemd is the thing that notices instead.
#
# Real correction from actually testing this (2026-08-31), not assumed:
# OnFailure= fires on EVERY failed run of the main service, including
# ones Restart=on-failure is about to retry on its own -- NOT only once
# StartLimitBurst is finally exhausted, which was the original (wrong)
# assumption here. Confirmed directly against a disposable test service:
# two transient crashes still eligible for retry each triggered
# OnFailure=, and only the third, genuinely-rate-limited failure should
# actually roll back. The guard below (`systemctl --user is-failed`,
# which only reports true once the unit has stopped being auto-restarted)
# is what makes this fire on a real crash LOOP specifically, not on the
# first ordinary blip Restart=on-failure would have recovered from
# unaided. Without it, one transient crash would trigger a rollback for
# no real reason.
#
# Second real correction from the same test session: reset-failed +
# start must NOT be unconditional ExecStartPost= directives -- those
# run after ANY successful ExecStart=, including the guard's early
# `exit 0` skip. That combination produced a real, observed runaway
# loop: skip (correct) -> ExecStartPost force-restarts the main service
# anyway -> it crashes again immediately -> OnFailure fires again ->
# skip -> force-restart... 13 cycles in ~16s in testing, completely
# bypassing Restart=on-failure/RestartSec's own pacing, and nothing
# about the loop was self-limiting. Fixed by folding reset-failed+start
# into the SAME conditional shell command, so they only run after an
# actual rollback, never after a guard skip.

[Service]
Type=oneshot
WorkingDirectory=__MIA_HOMESTEAD_ROOT__
ExecStart=/bin/bash -c '\
  systemctl --user is-failed mia-homestead.service >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0; \
  __MIA_HOMESTEAD_ROOT__/.venv/bin/python core/deploy_cli.py --db mia_homestead.db --emergency-rollback || exit 1; \
  systemctl --user reset-failed mia-homestead.service; \
  systemctl --user start mia-homestead.service \
'
